## Repair: `lib/pricing.js`

Original blob SHA: `8e5ba41a78e1d6a76c244d8ede57aba5a3cf9f29`

The only change is in `bundleDiscountCents`, where `quantity > 3` becomes `quantity >= 3`.

```js
// Prices and arithmetic stay in integer cents; the storefront never processes payments.
export const catalog = [
  { id: "arc", name: "Arc desk lamp", category: "LIGHTING", priceCents: 8900, color: "#d9c8b4", shape: "lamp", description: "A little warmth for your workspace." },
  { id: "loop", name: "Loop headphones", category: "AUDIO", priceCents: 12900, color: "#b4c4b5", shape: "headphones", description: "Make room for your own rhythm." },
  { id: "form", name: "Form notebook", category: "STATIONERY", priceCents: 2500, color: "#bdc5d4", shape: "notebook", description: "A place for your next good idea." },
  { id: "pour", name: "Pour carafe", category: "EVERYDAY", priceCents: 3900, color: "#e0c2b5", shape: "carafe", description: "The everyday, a little more considered." },
  { id: "rest", name: "Rest desk mat", category: "WORKSPACE", priceCents: 4900, color: "#bfc7bb", shape: "mat", description: "A softer landing for your working day." },
  { id: "hold", name: "Hold pen tray", category: "WORKSPACE", priceCents: 2900, color: "#d9ccad", shape: "tray", description: "Keep the small things together." }
];

export function shippingCents(subtotalCents) {
  if (!Number.isSafeInteger(subtotalCents) || subtotalCents < 0) throw new Error("Invalid subtotal");
  return subtotalCents === 0 || subtotalCents >= 5000 ? 0 : 799;
}

export function bundleDiscountCents(subtotalCents, quantity) {
  if (!Number.isSafeInteger(quantity) || quantity < 0) throw new Error("Invalid quantity");
  return quantity >= 3 ? Math.floor(subtotalCents * 0.1) : 0;
}

export function quote(lines) {
  if (!Array.isArray(lines) || lines.length > 50) throw new Error("Invalid cart");
  let subtotalCents = 0, quantity = 0;
  for (const line of lines) {
    const product = catalog.find((p) => p.id === line.id);
    if (!product || !Number.isSafeInteger(line.quantity) || line.quantity < 1 || line.quantity > 20) throw new Error("Invalid cart line");
    subtotalCents += product.priceCents * line.quantity;
    quantity += line.quantity;
  }
  const discountCents = bundleDiscountCents(subtotalCents, quantity);
  const deliveryCents = shippingCents(subtotalCents);
  return { subtotalCents, discountCents, shippingCents: deliveryCents, totalCents: subtotalCents - discountCents + deliveryCents, quantity };
}
```

## Rationale

- **Copy and tests agree:** `index.html` says "10% off bundles of 3+ items", and the test names the "exactly three items" case as earning the discount. The code's `> 3` excluded exactly three items, so the code was wrong and the tests and copy are left alone.
- **Both failures share this cause:**
  - `bundleDiscountCents(7500, 3)` now returns `floor(750.0) = 750`, not 0.
  - `quote([{id:"form",quantity:3}])` has subtotal 7500, discount 750 and shipping 0 (7500 ≥ 5000), so the total is 7500 − 750 + 0 = 6750.
- **Other assertions, traced by hand:**
  - `(5000, 2)` still gives 0, because 2 < 3.
  - `(7501, 4)` gives `floor(750.1) = 750`.
  - The `quote` deepEqual with two forms gives subtotal 5000, discount 0, shipping 0, total 5000, quantity 2. The `priceCents: 1` on the line is ignored because prices come from the catalog.
  - `shippingCents` is unchanged, so its boundary cases (0, 4999, 5000, 5001, -1, NaN) behave as before.
  - The invalid-quantity check in `bundleDiscountCents` is unchanged, so `(100, -1)` still throws.
- **Security gates:** the validation checks (cart size limit of 50, line quantity 1–20, integer checks) are untouched.

## Risks and missing evidence

- **Unverified:** this is a hand trace only. The repair is not confirmed until CI runs `node --test test/*.test.js` on the exact repair commit. Per the reviewed lesson, the `version.json` probe only shows the deployed SHA, not behaviour.
- **Other copies:** I did not search the repo for other hard-coded copies of the threshold, as the lesson advises. If other UI code or documentation states the discount rule, it was not examined.
- **Unrelated edge case, not changed:** `bundleDiscountCents` does not validate `subtotalCents`. It is only called from `quote` with a computed value, and no test requires a change.

